{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#130","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#130","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#130\",\"parent_revision\":\"e4cac0203247a114159e5187863e416bb01ed41d0bc5582da39ae102aa71796a\",\"root_revision\":\"e4cac0203247a114159e5187863e416bb01ed41d0bc5582da39ae102aa71796a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/agentskills-skilllint/skills/skilllint/references/rule-catalog.md` describes FM005 and FM006 as:\\n\\n- FM005 \u2014 \\\"name field contains invalid characters\\\"\\n- FM006 \u2014 \\\"description exceeds 1024 characters\\\"\\n\\nThe `ErrorCode` enum and `skilllint rules` say otherwise:\\n\\n- FM005 \u2014 field type mismatch\\n- FM006 \u2014 invalid field value\\n\\nThe catalog is hand-maintained and nothing enforces catalog\u2194registry consistency, so rows drift silently. This is the same class of failure that let FM008's meaning invert in `5a88d60` without a single consumer noticing for five months.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nGenerate the catalog from `RULE_REGISTRY`, or add a test asserting every catalog row matches the registered rule's code and summary.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- #124 \u2014 stub/emitter drift, same \\\"nothing enforces agreement\\\" shape\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"38b9c11587e2e547e91ce20cd384f164b9c4a47620ffc48155c6c24d501de898\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDORXxKvc8AAAABXP-b9w\"}"}